# The browser host's Wine root archive (site/wine.html): the paths, relative
# to the root scripts/wine-web.sh makes (Alpine's 386 Wine with winedraw
# and a prefix at /root/.wine), that `zig build web` packs into
# zig-out/web/wine.h9a for the demo page's ?wine mode.
#
# The files are the ones Wine opened, under strace, starting its desktop and
# each program the desktop has an icon for, and some DLLs their dialogs
# load (Open, Print, Help). Wine opens a DLL's copy in the prefix's
# system32, then loads its own from usr/lib/wine. The prefix's other copies,
# 190 MB of them, are left out. A path ending in / is an empty directory.

# Mount points, and where busybox --install puts its links.
dev/
proc/
sys/
tmp/
9/
mnt/term/cwd/
sbin/
usr/sbin/
usr/bin/

# busybox, for the page's start script.
bin/busybox

